{"name": "Apatosaurus", "clade": "apatosaurinae", "isd": false, "isnote": "", "sum": "Apatosaurus is a large, robust diplodocid sauropod from the Late Jurassic Morrison Formation of the western United States.", "wsnote": "Average adult length and mass of Apatosaurus louisae given by the cited Wikipedia revision; the same text says a larger specimen (OMNH 1670) was re-estimated in 2020 at about 30 m and 33 t by volumetric analysis.", "holotype": "Holotype of Apatosaurus ajax (named by Marsh in 1877); the specimen number was not read in the sources consulted for this draft.", "material": "Skeletons and skulls from the Morrison Formation of Colorado, Oklahoma, New Mexico, Wyoming and Utah; the skull was long confused with those of Camarasaurus and Brachiosaurus until 1909.", "completeness": "multiple", "exceptional": "", "biology": "Interpreted as a generalised browser that probably held its head raised; like other diplodocids its tail may have been used to make loud cracking sounds or, in a more recent suggestion, as a sensory organ.", "author": "Marsh 1877", "fad": 157.9, "lad": 143.1, "early": "Late Oxfordian", "late": "", "type_species": "Apatosaurus ajax", "pbdb_occ": 67, "species": [{"name": "Apatosaurus ajax", "author": "(Marsh 1877)", "fad": 154.8, "lad": 143.1, "interval": "Kimmeridgian–Tithonian", "ref": "original description"}, {"name": "Apatosaurus louisae", "author": "(Holland 1915)", "fad": 154.8, "lad": 143.1, "interval": "Kimmeridgian–Tithonian", "ref": ""}], "formations": [{"ids": ["morrison-united-states"], "formation": "Morrison", "group": "", "members": ["Brushy Basin", "Indian Fort", "Kenton", "Lake Como", "Salt Wash", "Talking Rocks", "Unit B"], "country": "United States", "regions": ["Arizona", "Colorado", "Montana", "New Mexico", "Oklahoma", "South Dakota", "Utah", "Wyoming"], "interval": "Late Oxfordian–Tithonian", "n": 67, "ma": [143.1, 157.9]}], "images": [{"kind": "skeletal", "file": "Apatosaurus louisae skeletal by Bricksmashtv.png", "src":